<title>SINGAPORE: Steamers Maritime buys two ships.</title>
<headline>Steamers Maritime buys two ships.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-09-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Steamers Maritime, part of conglomerate Keppel Corp said on Tuesday it has ordered two container ships at a total cost of US$34 million.</p>
<p>The 746-TEU vessels are from Jinling Shipyard in Nanjing, China, the company said in a statement.</p>
<p>They are due for delivery in 1998 and will raise Steamers' newbuilding orders from China to 10.</p>
<p>Steamers currently owns nine container ships.</p>
<p>--Singapore newsroom (65-8703080)</p>
